<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43994" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sesquĭ-pĕdālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of a foot and a half; one foot and a half</i> in
			length, breadth, or diameter, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 15,
				2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tigna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 4, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">talea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					5, 9, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mensura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					9, 15, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">11, 2, 18</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">11, 3, 48</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vitr.
				5, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 15,
				4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b> transf., to denote excessive length,
				<i>half a yard long</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					97, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. A.
					P. 97</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 7, 14, 10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
